<%# "My page" block.
    Redmine auto-discovers partials dropped under a plugin's app/views/my/blocks
    (Redmine::MyPage.additional_blocks); the selector's label comes from the
    my.blocks.redmine_quick_timelog i18n key. The chrome around it (the mypage-box div, sort
    handle, close button) is added by MyHelper#render_block: don't rebuild it here.
    Locals provided by Redmine: user, settings, block.

    The widget partial renders its own title (next to the timer-start button), so this
    file only needs a fallback title on the error path -- render_block hides a block
    whose content comes back blank, and an exception here would take down the whole
    "My page" view. %>
<% begin %>
  <%= render :partial => 'redmine_quick_timelog/widget' %>
<% rescue StandardError => e %>
  <h3><%= l(:redmine_quick_timelog_block_title) %></h3>
  <% Rails.logger.error("redmine_quick_timelog: could not render the \"My page\" block (#{e.class}: #{e.message})") %>
  <p class="nodata"><%= l(:redmine_quick_timelog_error_generic) %></p>
<% end %>
